course: dictionary
lesson: 10127
title: Thousandth: one part in a thousand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Thousandth has two jobs. As an adjective it tells you a place in a line: the thousandth visitor is the one who comes 1000th. As a noun it names one of a thousand equal parts: a thousandth is 1/1000, or 0.001.
explain: The words around it show which job it does. «Bladderworts suck in water fleas in less than a thousandth of a second.» A thousandth here is a tiny piece of a second, so it is the noun. Ask yourself: is this a place in a line, or one piece of a whole?
explain: Swap in your meaning to check it. «A typical bacterium is about 1 to 2 thousandths of a millimetre long.» Thousandths means more than one piece of a millimetre, and a millimetre is only a thousandth of a metre, so a bacterium is a tiny length. Your meaning fits, so you can trust it.
fact: Thousandth means 1000th in order, like the thousandth person in a queue.
fact: As a noun, a thousandth is one of a thousand equal parts: 1/1000, or 0.001.
fact: In decimals, the third digit after the decimal point is in the thousandths place: in 4.256, the 6 means six thousandths.
fact: A millimetre is a thousandth of a metre, and a millilitre is a thousandth of a litre.
fact: «For the thousandth time» is an everyday phrase meaning again and again, not a count of exactly one thousand.
exercise: «Bladderworts suck in water fleas in less than a thousandth of a second.» What does thousandth mean here? | *One of a thousand equal parts of a second | Half a second | The 1000th in a line | A very long time
exercise: In the number 4.256, what does the 6 mean? | Six tenths | *Six thousandths | Six hundreds | Six whole ones
exercise: Maya was the thousandth visitor through the gate, so she got a prize. What does thousandth mean here? | Very tiny | *The 1000th in order | Very quick | One of a thousand equal parts
test: «A typical bacterium is about 1 to 2 thousandths of a millimetre long.» A millimetre is a thousandth of what? | *A metre | A litre | A second | A kilogram
test: What is one thousandth written as a decimal? | *0.001 | 1.000 | 0.1 | 0.01
exam: What does «for the thousandth time» mean? | Very quickly | The last time ever | Exactly one thousand times | *Again and again
